{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ModularRayDiagonalPrune","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularRayDiagonalPrune","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularRayDiagonalPrune.inv_preserves_ray","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularRayDiagonalPrune.inv_preserves_ray","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularRayDiagonalPrune.lean#L80-L86","doc":"**The modular involution preserves the ray condition.** `b ↦ b⁻¹` maps\n`arg = π/4` to `arg = −π/4` — the other diagonal — and purely-imaginary\nsquares stay purely imaginary: the excluded locus is `b ↔ 1/b` symmetric,\nas the `Φ_b = Φ_{1/b}` self-duality requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularRayDiagonalPrune.imCV_zero_on_substrate_ray","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularRayDiagonalPrune.imCV_zero_on_substrate_ray","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularRayDiagonalPrune.lean#L65-L78","doc":"**The substrate ray is the diagonal.** If `b² ` is purely imaginary (the\n`2πb² = i·ln q₀` substrate condition), every real multiple of `b` lies on the\ndiagonal vanishing locus of the leading form: `Im 𝔙(b·t) = 0` for all real\n`t`. A real-scaling family along the substrate ray carries NO leading-order\n`S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularRayDiagonalPrune.imComplexVolume_eq_sq_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularRayDiagonalPrune.imComplexVolume_eq_sq_re","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularRayDiagonalPrune.lean#L56-L63","doc":"The corrected leading form reads off the real part of `u²`:\n`Re²u − Im²u = Re(u²)`. The diagonal locus `|Re u| = |Im u|` is exactly\n`Re(u²) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}